{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012FnMgoLctnWTZ9V49gyDXx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WN76djQWivoqzBArf7qbDa","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue review. Your focus is **methods and experiments**. Review the paper below using a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 6=Strong Accept; acceptance threshold ~25%).\n\n# Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** Per-Test Binary Classification for Execution-Free Code Verification: A Complexity-Dependent Reformulation\n\n**Core idea:** Reformulate execution-free code verification as per-test binary classification (CLS)—predict pass/fail per test without generating execution traces. Compare against Code World Models (CWM, generation-based) and trajectory-level scoring (TRAJ, single binary label per patch).\n\n**Dataset:** SWE-bench-PerTest — 438 instances, 87,600 test-level labels, 16 candidates each, 73/27 pass/fail ratio.\n\n**Key results:**\n- Table 2 (Repo-level CLS): Qwen3-4B 83.63%, Qwen3-8B 84.79%, DeepSeek-V2-Lite 74.20%, majority baseline 72.96%. Qwen F1 metrics are MISSING (dashes in table). DeepSeek: F1_macro=67.8, F1_pass=82.5, F1_fail=53.1.\n- Table 3 (Repo-level CWM): Qwen3-8B v12 unparseable=53.7%, v10=93%; DeepSeek unparseable=28%, overall acc=62.8%, parseable acc=66.3%. CLS-CWM gap: >15pp Qwen, 11.4pp DeepSeek.\n- Table 4 (DeepSeek func-level): CLS 86.93%, TRAJ seed42 83.24%, TRAJ seed123 85.08%. Only N=2 seeds. Caveat about unfixed evaluation pipeline with potential data leakage.\n- Section 3.5 (CLS≈TRAJ Qwen3): Pooled gap −0.40pp, 95% CI [−1.32, +0.52], TOST p=0.007, ±2pp margin. 5 seeds, 114 clusters, 10K bootstrap resamples. ICC=0.191, DEFF=3.97.\n- Table 5 (Re-repair): Control 0.215, CLS-Diag 0.225 (+1.0pp, p=0.62), Oracle-Diag 0.285 (+7.0pp), Random-Diag 0.175 (−4.0pp). N=200 instances, 5 repair attempts each.\n\n**Missing experiments acknowledged:**\n- DeepSeek repo-level TRAJ (2 seeds): not completed\n- DeepSeek func-level TRAJ (fixed evaluation): data leakage bug unresolved\n\n**Experiment design reference (from review_context.yaml):**\nThe planned experiments included: diagnostic-rerepair, swebench-pertest-data, deepseek-cls-repo, deepseek-cwm-repo, deepseek-traj-repo (NOT COMPLETED), deepseek-traj-repo-s123 (NOT COMPLETED), deepseek-traj-func-v2-fixed (FAILED_TO_RESOLVE), deepseek-traj-func-v2-s123-fixed (FAILED_TO_RESOLVE).\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate:\n1. **Methodological soundness** — Are the formulations well-defined? Are comparisons controlled and fair? Is the statistical methodology appropriate?\n2. **Experimental rigor** — Are there enough seeds/runs? Are baselines adequate? Are the missing experiments critical? Is the data leakage concern adequately addressed?\n3. **Results interpretation** — Are claims appropriately scoped? Do the numbers support the claims? Are caveats sufficient?\n4. **Reproducibility** — Is there enough detail to reproduce?\n\nProvide:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, with severity: minor/moderate/major/critical)\n- Questions for Authors (bulleted)\n- Missing Experiments Assessment: which planned experiments are missing and how much this hurts\n- Score (1-6) with confidence (low/medium/high)\n- Short recommendation sentence\n\nKeep your review under 800 words."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18697,"cache_read_input_tokens":23648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18697},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1d10b2a-da1c-4436-8566-b8bd50259b88","uuid":"155a95d6-931d-44f2-a515-c988a7c6d0bd"}
